jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_2026-08-31 — content-adaptive predictor selection
for the SECTIONED per-group tree learns (imazen/jxl-encoder#99 item 1, T3).

Host: mac (aarch64 laptop, 12 cores). Encoder: release, default features +
`std parallel profile-phases`. Reference: cjxl v0.12.0 [_NEON_BF16_,NEON].
Harness: `jxl-encoder/examples/sectioned_k_corpus.rs` (features / render /
sweep / phases / croptl) + `scripts/select_sectioned_k_corpus.py` +
`scripts/fit_sectioned_k_gate.py` + `scripts/sectioned_k_bar_cell.sh`.
NO `-C target-cpu=native` anywhere.


================================================================ FILES

jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_corpus_2026-08-31.tsv   the corpus: 310 renditions
    of 52 origins, with each rendition's sha256 AND its origin's sha256, the
    cluster it represents, its split, and how it was derived (crop|resize,
    target size). This is the reproducibility record for the fit.
jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_picks_2026-08-31.tsv    the (origin, cluster, split,
    kind, target) rows the renderer consumed — i.e. the clustering's output.
jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_2026-08-31.tsv          full corpus x 6 arms at
    e7 t=8 (310 x 6 = 1860 encodes). BYTES are the load-bearing column here.
jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_t1_2026-08-31.tsv       the >= 1 MP subset x 4 arms
    at e7 t=1 (122 x 4 = 488 encodes). WALL is the load-bearing column here.
jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_leaves{,_t1}_2026-08-31.tsv  probe-tree leaf count
    per rendition, distilled from `JXL_PROBE_COSTS=1`. The fit script takes
    these directly, so the fit re-runs from the repo with no re-encode.
jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_bar_2026-08-31.tsv      the wall BAR cell (photo
    3840x2160) at e7 and e9, threads 1 and 8, 5 repeats, ours vs cjxl.

Re-run the fit:
    python3 scripts/fit_sectioned_k_gate.py \
      benchmarks/jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_2026-08-31.tsv \
      benchmarks/jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_leaves_2026-08-31.tsv


================================================================ THE CORPUS

The owner made corpus expansion a precondition, because the prior K sweep
(`jxl_sectioned_prune_k_2026-08-28`) had THREE images.

Pool: all 2233 imazen-26 `png-v3` images across 21 content folders, plus the
5 gb82-sc screens the 2026-08-28 benchmark used (2238 total).

Representative selection is by CLUSTERING, not sampling. imazen-26 is
heavily skewed — 749 of 2233 images are AI product shots and another 370 are
web screenshots — so a random draw reproduces that skew and drops exactly the
outliers a content gate fails on. `sectioned_k_corpus features` computes a
10-dimensional content vector per image (flat-run mass, gradient-zero rate,
unique colours per pixel, activity-context distribution and its entropy,
best-static-predictor bits/px, root-cost spread, per-context winner count and
mismatch mass — the axes predictor choice actually depends on), and
`select_sectioned_k_corpus.py` runs k-means++ (K=24, 8 restarts, seed
20260830, best inertia 2059.1) over the standardized vectors and takes the
TWO members nearest each centroid.

Split is by ORIGIN: of each cluster's two representatives, one goes to
`train` and one to `validate`, so every rendition of an origin lands on the
same side and no derivative of a training image can appear in validation,
while both sides still span every content region. The 5 gb82-sc screens are
carried as a third split, `continuity`; they are reported separately and are
NOT part of the fit.

Cluster sizes (n = pool members assigned, rep = the train-side pick):
   0: 178  1400-lilith-nature (photo, foliage)
   1: 212  9226-ai-products/toys
   2:  64  7000-plots/random-charts
   3:   1  9226-ai-products/home/decor (5504x3072 — a genuine singleton
           outlier, kept rather than dropped)
   4:  40  6000-scans-patents (1-bit original scans)
   5: 140  9000-ai-clipart
   6:  67  1000-photos-general (night, high ISO)
   7: 134  6600-ia-scans-manuscript-illustrations
   8:   8  8100-web-screenshots (1440x900 / 1920x1080)
   9:  29  9226-ai-products/home/small-appliances
  10: 172  9226-ai-products/grocery
  11:  34  5000-nps-brochures (grayscale maps)
  12:  29  5000-nps-brochures (grayscale, second mode)
  13: 119  9226-ai-products/whitelabeled-beauty
  14:  88  9226-ai-products/clothing-womens
  15:  11  7000-plots/real-charts
  16: 195  1400-lilith-nature (landscape)
  17:  67  9226-ai-products/sporting-goods
  18: 197  9226-ai-products/clothing-loungewear
  19:  50  9226-ai-products/with-callouts
