The positive t=8 wall column on that table is NOT the bar cell. It is the
corpus mean at 8 threads over renditions that top out at 4 MP, where the
probe's ~200 ms is a large share of a ~1 s encode. At t=1 the same cells are
-16 %, and at 8.3 MP the t=8 cell is a win too (see the bar table). The
crossover is size, and it is reported rather than averaged away.


================================================================ THE BAR CELL

`jxl_sectioned_adaptive_k_bar_2026-08-31.tsv`. Photo 3840x2160 (imazen-26
1403 `nature_large-tree-canopy`, cropped TOP-LEFT, sha256
0e72993af2f43ba978b5f2cbb3e630dc4c537ea615de4fd9c3aa5734c67821c9), the cell
issue #99 quotes. `SectionedTrees::On` both sides. 5 repeats, arms
INTERLEAVED inside each rep. MIN over repeats:

| cell | cjxl v0.12 | K=8 (before) | gate (after) | gate vs K=8 | bytes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| e7 t=1 | 7.22 s | 11.52 s (1.60x) | **8.90 s (1.23x)** | -22.7 % | +0.315 % |
| e7 t=8 | 1.10 s | 1.96 s (1.78x) | 1.80 s (1.64x) | -7.9 % | +0.315 % |
| e9 t=1 | 41.97 s | 44.79 s (1.07x) | **33.14 s (0.79x)** | -26.0 % | +0.263 % |
| e9 t=8 | 6.07 s | 6.78 s (1.12x) | **5.85 s (0.96x)** | -13.8 % | +0.263 % |

**e7 t=1 meets the <= 1.3x bar. Both e9 cells meet it and now BEAT cjxl.
e7 t=8 does not, and no predictor-set change reaches it**: fixed K=4 — the
maximum possible reduction, and a byte regression on palette content — was
measured at 1729 ms on this cell, i.e. **1.38x**, against a 1.3x target of
1430 ms. The remaining t=8 gap is #99's other named lever (a cheaper split
search over the kept set), plus the structural fact that the probe's ~200 ms
is 10 % of a 1.8 s encode at t=8 and 8 % of an 8.9 s encode at t=1.

Wall conventions: `cjxl` is whole-process wall INCLUDING PNG decode (the
convention #99 used); ours is encode-only. At t=1 the PNG load is noise; at
t=8 it is ~10 % of cjxl's number, so the t=8 ratios above FLATTER us and the
true e7 t=8 standing is worse than 1.64x.

Repeat spread on this host (max/min): e7 t=1 0.2-0.6 %, e9 t=1 3-4 %, and
**t=8 cells 7-36 %** — which is why the t=8 rows are min-over-repeats and why
the arms are interleaved.

METHOD TRAP, recorded because it inverted a sign: the first run of this table
did 5 repeats of K=8 and then 5 of the gate. Block-ordered like that it
reported the gate **+10.4 % SLOWER** at e7 t=8. Interleaving reports **-7.9 %**
(and a separate 9-repeat interleaved run agrees at -8.7 %). Short
multi-threaded cells drift over a run; do not block-order them.

Phase split on the same cell (`sectioned_k_corpus phases`, e7 t=1), which
also re-verifies the root cause #99 filed:

  arm      total      learn   find_best_split   probe    gather
  K=8     11540 ms   8654 ms      4827 ms         -      892 ms
  gate     8954 ms   4808 ms      2829 ms      683 ms    704 ms
